data: {"type": "answer_chunk", "data": "{\"type\": \"citation_found\", \"passage_id\": \"77d083cc-072a-588d-b5f7-59251a605a30\", \"excerpt\": \"57. That extraordinary events sometimes appear to human beings has been reported even by Greeks -- not only those who might be suspected of myth-making, but also those who have demonstrated at length genuine philosophizing and a truth-loving exposition of what came to their attention. Such accounts we have read in Chrysippus of Soli, some in Pythagoras, and also in certain more recent writers of y\", \"node_ids\": [], \"confidence\": 0.7, \"work_label\": \"Contre Celse, Livre II\"}"}

